From 94b0078f80a05dfc0622165636d4d944037fdb58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mercurious <dutch.money@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:30:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ir3/ra: fix the forced-double-threadsize register cap (8
 slots per vec4, not 16)

When an app requires a subgroup size of 2 * threadsize_base with full
subgroups (VkPipelineShaderStageRequiredSubgroupSizeCreateInfo = 128 plus
REQUIRE_FULL_SUBGROUPS on a6xx), Turnip compiles with real_wavesize =
IR3_DOUBLE_ONLY, and ir3_ra_get_reg_file_limits() is supposed to cap full
register pressure so a double-size wave still fits in the register file.

The cap was computed as reg_size_vec4 / 2 * 16, but limit_pressure.full is
counted in half-register slots, 8 per vec4 (RA_FULL_SIZE = 4 * 48 * 2).
On gens with reg_size_vec4 = 64 (A650 / a6xx_gen3 and friends) that is
512 slots, above RA_FULL_SIZE (384), so the MIN2 never lowers anything.
RA is then free to use all 48 vec4 in a double-threadsize shader, which
needs 96 vec4 per wave-pair from a 64 vec4 file: the shader reports
"0 max_waves, 1 double_threadsize" and computes garbage.

Observed with llama.cpp's Vulkan backend on A650 (Mesa 26.1.6 .. 26.3-devel):
mul_mat_vec shaders with NUM_COLS >= 4 (one subgroupAdd reduction per
column, each accumulating via OPC_SCAN_MACRO) cross the 32 vec4 line,
compile to 48 full regs / 0 max_waves, and return wrong results
(test-backend-ops MUL_MAT f32 m=16 n=4..8 k=256: ERR ~40..1500).
n=1..3 (2 max_waves) and every wave64 variant are correct.

Use reg_size_vec4 / 2 * 4 * 2, the same vec4 -> slot conversion as
calc_limit_pressure_for_cs_with_barrier(). a7xx (reg_size_vec4 = 96) is
unaffected: 96 / 2 * 8 = 384 = RA_FULL_SIZE, as before.
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
index e15a79b..1d302c1 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
@@ -2788,10 +2788,19 @@ ir3_ra_get_reg_file_limits(struct ir3_shader_variant *v)
    /* If the user forces a doubled threadsize, we may have to lower the limit
     * because on some gens the register file is not big enough to hold a
     * double-size wave with all 48 registers in use.
+    *
+    * A double-size wave needs 2 * max_reg vec4 of the reg_size_vec4 file, so
+    * at most reg_size_vec4 / 2 vec4 per fiber. limit_pressure.full counts
+    * half-register slots (RA_FULL_SIZE = 48 vec4 * 4 comps * 2), i.e. 8 per
+    * vec4 -- the same conversion calc_limit_pressure_for_cs_with_barrier()
+    * uses. The previous "* 16" doubled the cap: with reg_size_vec4 = 64
+    * (a6xx gen1-gen4, e.g. A650) it came out as 512 > RA_FULL_SIZE and never
+    * applied, so RA could hand out all 48 vec4, giving max_waves = 0 and a
+    * shader whose registers alias across the wave-pair.
     */
    if (v->shader_options.real_wavesize == IR3_DOUBLE_ONLY) {
       limit_pressure.full =
-         MIN2(limit_pressure.full, v->compiler->reg_size_vec4 / 2 * 16);
+         MIN2(limit_pressure.full, v->compiler->reg_size_vec4 / 2 * 4 * 2);
    }
 
    assert(limit_pressure.full <= RA_FULL_SIZE);
-- 
2.55.0

